WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:25.196 --> 00:00:30.035
The ovaries
are the female reproductive glands.

00:00:30.035 --> 00:00:32.566
They consist of three types of cells:

00:00:32.566 --> 00:00:34.546
epithelial,

00:00:34.546 --> 00:00:36.406
germ,

00:00:36.406 --> 00:00:38.986
and stromal.

00:00:40.666 --> 00:00:43.375
When the cells in the ovaries
grow abnormally,

00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:49.497
they develop into tumors
that can be noncancerous or cancerous.

00:00:49.497 --> 00:00:52.056
If cancerous tumors
are not detected early,

00:00:52.056 --> 00:00:53.556
the cancer cells can spread

00:00:53.556 --> 00:00:56.218
from the ovaries
throughout the pelvic region

00:00:56.218 --> 00:01:01.568
and continue to spread
to the abdominal area and other organs.

00:01:01.568 --> 00:01:03.666
Determining the stage of ovarian cancer

00:01:03.666 --> 00:01:08.028
is very important
in developing a treatment plan.

00:01:08.028 --> 00:01:13.717
At stage one, cancer is limited
to one or both of the ovaries.

00:01:13.717 --> 00:01:20.076
In stage two, ovarian cancer extends
to the pelvis area.

00:01:20.076 --> 00:01:21.378
In stage three,

00:01:21.378 --> 00:01:26.169
ovarian cancer has spread
to the abdominal region.

00:01:26.169 --> 00:01:30.349
In stage four, ovarian cancer extends
into the liver,

00:01:30.349 --> 00:01:35.290
or to locations
beyond the abdominal area.

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:38.119
Ovarian cancer treatment
typically includes

00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:40.381
surgery,

00:01:40.381 --> 00:01:43.071
chemotherapy,

00:01:43.071 --> 00:01:45.691
radiation therapy,

00:01:45.691 --> 00:01:49.379
or a combination of therapies.

00:01:50.459 --> 00:01:52.979
[no sound]

